      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CAPTAIN SHUFFLES (8) was runner-up to the mighty Leap To Fame when resuming then relished his absence last start, leading to score by 6.5m at this circuit and distance. Kept up to the mark with an easy trial win so should have come on further. Draws on the back row but should enjoy an early trail and is good enough to win from there. ATTACHMENT (1) has had seven weeks off since he was beaten into third as a hot favourite last start but has won a trial in that time. Had been flying with four straight wins here prior and has the speed to take advantage of the ace draw. TIGER BAND WAGON (4) won from wider here three back and has been ticking along well since, coming from this barrier to place last week. TIMS A TROOPER (6) could be working his way back into form having gone close last week.",
